# The lantern's two tile layers. What makes it worth a map is in
# `Map0005.json`: a parallel event lays `Picture/Night` over it, a dark
# mask with a cone of light, fixed to the map at transparency 35. The two
# trees are under the mask, and the one at (10, 5) is in the cone: their
# crowns are the layer above the hero, which the mask has to shade too.
# `tests/test_map_picture.py`.

# 20x15, 300 tiles per layer
# The two tile layers, in reading order: one id per tile, 20 per line.
# These are the ids the binary stores; what turns them into pictures is
# the chipset. Edited by hand, the count has to stay the same.
